*reset*

1. git reset (go to the previous stage)
2. git reset --hard

*stage*

1. git add -all / git add -A (all things are added to the stage)
2. git add . (current directory is added to the stage )
3. git add * (All except Delete are in the stage.)  ***question***
4.git add myFolder/three.txt (myFolder/three.txt, *.txt)

*commit*

1. git commit -m "I changed my file"
(
Before commit,
  git config --global user.email "you@example.com"
  git config --global user.name "Your Name"
)
2. git reset HEAD~

*remove rm*
1. git rm two.txt (It removes the item and also add in stage)
2. git rm two.txt -f (if you change the file content. It forcefully removes the item.)
3.git rm --cached two.txt(it don't delete from your directory. But in stage it is delete)
4. git rm -r " folderName " (for delete folder. Mean recursively delete a folder)

*Checkout, Branching & Merging*

1.git branch
2.git branch "branch name" (initialy clone of main branch.)
3.git branch -M main (for rename the branch)
4.git checkout "branch name"
5.git merge main -m "marge it with main"
6.git branch -a(see the hidden file)

*Fetch, Pull & Push*

1.git push origin main
(Before push anything type "git config --global credential.helper store")
2.git fetch && git merge == git pull

